{"event_schema": "1.0.0", "run_id": "e9a06d0b-4595-47b7-8eb0-54e5233a4de1", "seq": 48, "event_type": "model_response", "utc": "2026-09-26T00:54:02.415465Z", "monotonic_ms": 69133, "case_id": "case_006", "provider": "anthropic", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "turn_index": 10, "duration_ms": 12706, "content": "{\"tool\": \"disposition\", \"args\": {\"category\": \"ward\", \"urgency\": \"urgent\", \"rationale\": \"This 38-year-old woman probably has primary adrenal insufficiency. The likely cause is tuberculous adrenalitis. CT shows bilateral calcified adrenal nodules and old lung and pleural TB lesions (imaging_007). She has hyperpigmentation over the finger joints and knees (hpi_001, physical_exam_003). She had a chest opacity 5 years ago that was never diagnosed or treated as TB (pmh_002). She has no fever, night sweats or cough. The source did not report her vital signs, cortisol, ACTH, electrolytes, glucose, renin or IGRA, so we cannot confirm the diagnosis, check how severe it is, or rule out imminent adrenal crisis. Hydrocortisone 15 mg/day was started before confirmation, so it could mask the results of later tests. Because of this uncertainty, she should be admitted for monitored assessment and treatment rather than discharged.\", \"followup_or_handoff\": \"Admit to the medical or endocrinology ward. Check vital signs and orthostatic BP now and monitor them. Send stat sodium, potassium, glucose, creatinine, cortisol and ACTH, and renin and aldosterone. Draw these before the next hydrocortisone dose if possible, or do a cosyntropin stimulation test with a dexamethasone bridge if confirmation is still needed. If she shows hypotension, hyponatremia, hyperkalemia or hypoglycemia, treat as adrenal crisis: hydrocortisone 100 mg IV bolus plus IV normal saline. Add fludrocortisone if renin is high or she has mineralocorticoid deficiency. Screen for active TB with IGRA, sputum AFB smear, culture and NAAT, and chest imaging review. Consult infectious disease about anti-TB therapy. Rifampicin roughly doubles hydrocortisone needs, so raise the hydrocortisone dose if it is started. Consider histoplasmosis serology and antigen to exclude fungal causes. Teach sick-day rules, give an emergency injectable hydrocortisone kit and a medical alert ID, and arrange endocrinology follow-up.\"}}", "tool_transport": "json_emulated", "tool_calls_count": 1, "provider_metadata": {"transport": "claude_code_subscription_cli_json_action", "tool_transport": "json_emulated", "subtype": "success", "model_requested": "claude-opus-5-5", "models_reported": ["claude-opus-5-5"], "effort_requested": "high", "cost_estimate_usd": 0.06778680000000001, "assistant_note": "", "temperature_accepted": false, "seed_accepted": false, "max_output_tokens_accepted": false}}
